{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Six covered wagons.</b> צַב means nothing but covered, as in ״וּבַצַּבִּים וּבַפְּרָדִים״ (Isaiah 66); wagons that are covered are called צַבִּים." "<b>And they brought them before the Tent of Meeting.</b> Moses did not accept them from their hand until he was told so from the mouth of the Omnipresent. Rabbi Natan said: What did the princes see to volunteer here first, while for the work of the Mishkan they did not volunteer first? Rather — thus the princes said: let the congregation volunteer whatever they volunteer, and whatever they lack, we will make up. Once they saw that the congregation had made up everything, as it says ״וְהַמְּלָאכָה הָיְתָה דַיָּם״ (Exodus 36), they said: from now what is there for us to do? They brought the shoham stones and the settings for the ephod and the breastplate. Therefore they volunteered here first (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:47.458842219Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}